            "required_age": 0,
            "is_free": false,
            "detailed_description": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/497670/extras/871a7a7d6e4342a204c3d2f38109cb87.avif?t=1782163953\" width=616 height=135 /></span><br>Line/Dash is an Arcade-oriented game that doubles as a procedural player-controlled multimedia sculpture.<br>The basic gameplay is extremely simple, and only requires two buttons: the left click of your mouse will drop lines from the sky, while the right click will make those lines dash forward.<br>As the pace of the opposition gets faster and the line start splitting and crossing Line/Dash becomes a hypnotic and ever-changing visual experience.<br>Are you ready to put your reflexes through its paces in the middle of a deluge of arrows, sounds and neon colors?<br>Due to a very cool and custom audio compartment, this Rez-like game will falbbergast you without any doubt!<br><br><strong>Features:</strong><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/497670/extras/a13c88c2f46d6aae539d318252b5b21d.webp?t=1782163953\" width=16 height=16 /></span> Immediate gameplay, just two buttons to drop lines from the sky and make them dash forward<br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/497670/extras/a13c88c2f46d6aae539d318252b5b21d.webp?t=1782163953\" width=16 height=16 /></span> Intriguing music and sfx perfectly fiting with the ever-increasing speed of the gameplay<br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/497670/extras/a13c88c2f46d6aae539d318252b5b21d.webp?t=1782163953\" width=16 height=16 /></span> Neon-like colors and vintage, arcade look, with a little modern twist<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >\t<strong>WARNING </strong></h2><strong>Lots of contrasting bright colors, if you have problems with that stuff maybe don't play it</strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >\t<strong>Controller Support</strong></h2><strong>The game is fully playable with a controller after setting it up in the initial launcher. It will still need keybord/mouse support to get through the launcher</strong>",
