                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "You control lines using two buttons. The left button creates a line, while the right button directs it toward the squares. You must hit the targets before they reach the left edge of the screen. Each miss costs you one of your three lives; once they are all gone, you receive your final score\n\n✅Neon aesthetic vibrant colors, geometric shapes, and a shifting background create an attractive, almost hypnotic visual effect\n✅The action accelerates over time, making it increasingly difficult to hit the incoming squares\n✅Intriguing artistic effect the lines that remain on the screen form colorful compositions, reminiscent of a multimedia sculpture\n✅The price is reasonable\n\n❌Limited variety the game lacks additional mechanics, game modes, or new challenges (it’s a short-lived experience)\n\n✅✅ Verdict: [strike] Terrible [/strike], [strike] Bad [/strike], [strike] Mediocre [/strike], [b] Decent [/b], [strike] Good [/strike], [strike] Very Good [/strike] (Rating scale for short games, retro indie simulators, and similar titles)\n\n[quote] If you'd like to see more of my reviews, you can find them on my\ncurator page:\n[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45994324/admin/reviews_manage/]CuratorKingViking[/url]\nand in my group:\n[url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/CuratorKingViking]GroupKingViking[/url]\n\nIf you have any questions about my reviews, feel free to ask.\nI'm happy to answer them. All reviews are my own!!\nBest regards, King Viking Bezimienny, Polish Game Reviewer. [/quote]",
